98118	98298	98111	98111	she	2900	“ Indeed you mistake me . I am not a sad , melancholy creature . I am never unhappy long together . I am angry and naughty — not like Celia : I have a great outburst , and then all seems glorious again . I can not help believing in glorious things in a blind sort of way . I should be quite willing to enjoy the art here , but there is so much that I do n’t know the reason of — so much that seems to me a consecration of ugliness rather than beauty . The painting and sculpture may be wonderful , but the feeling is often low and brutal , and sometimes even ridiculous . Here and there I see what takes me at once as noble — something that I might compare with the Alban Mountains or the sunset from the Pincian Hill ; but that makes it the greater pity that there is so little of the best kind among all that mass of things over which men have toiled so . ”
